   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\), \\( g \\), and \\( h \\) are continuous for all real numbers, with \\( f(0) = 0 \\), \\( f(1) = 3 \\), \\( f(2) = 2 \\), \\( f(3) = 4 \\), \\( f(4) = 2 \\), \\( g(0) = 1 \\), \\( g(1) = 3 \\), \\( g(2) = 1 \\), \\( g(3) = 3 \\), \\( g(4) = 2 \\), \\( h(0) = 0 \\), \\( h(1) = 4 \\), \\( h(2) = 1 \\), \\( h(3) = 3 \\), \\( h(4) = 0 \\). Find the value of \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} g(f(h(x))) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 1
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Each function is continuous, so the innermost limit is a function value: \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} h(x) = h(1) = 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Work outward. \\( f \\) is continuous at 4, so \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} f(h(x)) = f(4) = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "\\( g \\) is continuous at 2, so the limit of the composite is \\( g(2) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      }
   ],
